useum landmark suited to a low-key meetup.","evidence_claim":"The North Dakota Heritage Center identifies the Northern Lights Atrium as a museum space combining architecture and symbolism; admission is free every day.","source_url":"https://statemuseum.nd.gov/about/facility","source_title":"About the Facility | North Dakota Heritage Center & State Museum","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"At 612 East Boulevard Avenue. Admission is free every day; follow posted museum rules.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ndhc-pembina-river-plaza","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Pembina River Plaza","title":"Walk the Pembina River Plaza","subtitle":"North Dakota Heritage Center & State Museum grounds","notes":"Step outside to inspect the geological specimens, then loop back into the museum without needing to make this a long outdoor commitment.","short_summary":"An outdoor plaza with specimens from the state’s geologic past.","evidence_claim":"The outdoor Pembina River Plaza features specimens from North Dakota’s geologic past, and the Heritage Center states that admission is free every day.","source_url":"https://statemuseum.nd.gov/about/facility","source_title":"About the Facility | North Dakota Heritage Center & State Museum","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"On the museum grounds at 612 East Boulevard Avenue. Admission is free every day; dress for weather.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ndhc-corridor-of-history","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Corridor of History","title":"Follow the Corridor of History tracks","subtitle":"North Dakota Heritage Center & State Museum","notes":"Walk the corridor in chronological order and look down for changing tracks, from dinosaur prints to moccasins